Subject: [PATCH] rapier - 1.8 combat: allow crits while sprinting

1.9 added !isSprinting() to the player crit condition. 1.8.9's crit
check (fallDistance > 0, airborne, not on ladder, not in water, no
blindness, not riding) never tested sprint state, so sprint + falling
always crit. removing the gate restores sprint-crits and with it the
1.8 W-tap crit combo game.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/player/Player.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/player/Player.java
index aaa6f0954ca09766c73a1e4957333f0daa89f713..32d809d7fdf1d3a12f2ee9ba65b03d2728013c29 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/player/Player.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/player/Player.java
@@ -1128,8 +1128,7 @@ public abstract class Player extends Avatar implements ContainerUser {
             && !this.isInWater()
             && !this.isMobilityRestricted()
             && !this.isPassenger()
-            && target instanceof LivingEntity
-            && !this.isSprinting();
+            && target instanceof LivingEntity; // rapier - 1.8 combat: sprint crits. the !isSprinting() gate was added in 1.9; 1.8.9's crit check (EntityPlayer.attackTargetEntityWithCurrentItem) never tested sprint state, so sprint + falling = crit
     }
 
     private boolean isSweepAttack(boolean isStrong, boolean isCritical, boolean extraKnockback) {
